browser_plan:
Build a Vite + React 19 page at demo.milliseconds.ai/inbox-blitz. Keep the Gmail-shaped layout (lane nav, list, reader, stats rail) but restyle with the milliseconds design tokens and fonts from ~/projects/cloudraker-spring-2026 (DESIGN.md, apps/milliseconds). Copy src/data, src/lib and the tests as-is; drop server/jev.ts and the NDJSON streaming. Proxy: one Cloudflare Worker route /api/dm1/:route that forwards the JSON body to https://api.milliseconds.ai/v1/decision-machine-1/:route with the server-side bearer key, allow-lists the 8 route names, caps body at 32 texts, and passes back status, body, x-inference-ms and x-input-tokens. The key never reaches the browser. Client: a small queue (src/lib/dm1Queue.ts) that releases one request every 500 ms (2 req/s) and runs at most 2 in flight. Each email becomes text = `From: ${from} <${fromEmail}>
Subject: ${subject}

${body}`; chunk into batches of 32. Triage: for each batch send the 7 route calls in the queue in this order: classify, then the four yes-no statements, then the two rate calls, so lanes populate early; merge the seven results into one Judgment per email and patch the row when the seventh lands. Intent label: one yes-no call per batch with the intent statement, 16 calls per intent, about 8 s; update matches as each batch returns and keep the existing 50 ms UI tick. Default the demo to the first 128 emails (4 batches, 28 triage requests, about 14 s) with a "Triage all 500" toggle (112 requests, about 56 s) so the full pass stays under the 1M tokens/min org budget. On HTTP 429 the queue pauses for retry-after (default 5 s), shows a banner "Shared demo limit reached, resuming in Ns", and resumes from the same batch; the proxy returns 429 unchanged. Stats rail uses x-inference-ms for p50/p95 and x-input-tokens for tokens and cost; label the throughput as emails per second, not requests. Keep keyboard shortcuts and the keyword-rules comparison; they run in the browser only.
